WEBVTT

00:09:27.836 --> 00:09:30.476
so that we could begin the process
of plaster jacketing.

00:09:30.476 --> 00:09:33.396
So those white bits you can see
in the image, that's not snow,

00:09:33.436 --> 00:09:36.156
although it was very cold
a few days on site,

00:09:36.156 --> 00:09:37.676
that's actually plaster.

00:09:37.676 --> 00:09:41.876
Plaster jacketing is an important process
in the field of paleontology.

00:09:42.396 --> 00:09:44.516
We use these protective plaster jackets

00:09:44.556 --> 00:09:49.556
that essentially care for and secure
the bones and the surrounding matrix

00:09:49.556 --> 00:09:52.436
so that we can take them
out of the field and into the lab

00:09:52.476 --> 00:09:55.316
so that we can analyze
the fossil and the matrix

00:09:55.356 --> 00:09:56.876
and work out what's going on.

00:09:56.916 --> 00:10:00.476
We also had to, for the bigger
skull block and the body block,